  "id": "family-psychology",
  "term": "family psychology",
  "definition": "Family psychology is the study of how family relationships and household life are shaped by wider social and cultural expectations. It looks at how norms and identities become family rules, power patterns, and emotional climates, and how family experiences can in turn reinforce, soften, or challenge those norms.",
